      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-290808",
      ":question/problem": "The function $f$ is defined by\n$f(x) = (x + 2)(x - 3)(x - 7)$.\nThe function $g$ is defined by $g(x) = f(x + 2)$. The graph of $y = g(x)$ in the $xy$-plane has $x$-intercepts at $(a, 0), (b, 0)$, and $(c, 0)$, where $a, b$, and $c$ are distinct constants.\n\nWhat is the value of $a + b + c$?"
