      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-323688",
      ":question/problem": "A function $f$ is defined by\n$f(x) = (x - 3)(x + 2)(x + 8)$.\nDefine $h$ by $h(x) = f(x - 4)$. The graph $y = h(x)$ has $x$-intercepts at $(p, 0)$, $(q, 0)$, and $(r, 0)$, where $p > q > r$ are distinct constants. What is the value of $p + q + r$?"
